msgid "Background {#background}"
msgstr "Background {#background}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Julia is a dynamic programming language designed primarily for numerical and scientific computing. Its high-performance numerical computing capabilities make it a natural fit for quantum simulation workflows. In this tutorial, we show how Julia is used for both classical pre- and post-processing (for example, building Hamiltonians, running ODE (ordinary differential equation) solvers, and computing expectation values) and for orchestrating quantum hardware jobs, eliminating the need to switch between languages or environments.\n"
msgstr "Ang Julia ay isang dynamic na programming language na pangunahing dinisenyo para sa numerical at scientific computing. Dahil sa mataas nitong performance sa numerical computing, natural itong akma sa mga workflow ng quantum simulation. Sa tutorial na ito, ipinapakita namin kung paano ginagamit ang Julia kapwa para sa classical na pre- at post-processing (halimbawa, pagbuo ng mga Hamiltonian, pagpapatakbo ng mga ODE (ordinary differential equation) solver, at pagkalkula ng mga expectation value) at para sa pag-orchestrate ng mga quantum hardware job, na inaalis ang pangangailangang magpalipat-lipat sa pagitan ng mga wika o environment.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To interface with IBM Quantum&reg; hardware from Julia, this tutorial uses two packages from the Qiskit ecosystem: `Qiskit.jl` wraps the Qiskit C library and provides circuit construction and transpilation functionality in Julia; `QiskitIBMRuntime.jl` connects to IBM Quantum hardware through the IBM Quantum Compute Service client, enabling job submission and result retrieval directly from Julia.\n"
msgstr "Para makipag-interface sa IBM Quantum&reg; hardware mula sa Julia, gumagamit ang tutorial na ito ng dalawang package mula sa Qiskit ecosystem: ang `Qiskit.jl` ay bumabalot sa Qiskit C library at nagbibigay ng circuit construction at transpilation functionality sa Julia; ang `QiskitIBMRuntime.jl` ay kumokonekta sa IBM Quantum hardware sa pamamagitan ng IBM Quantum Compute Service client, na nagbibigay-daan sa job submission at result retrieval nang direkta mula sa Julia.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In this tutorial, we consider the trotterized evolution of the transverse-field Ising model on a 1D chain with nearest-neighbor interactions:\n"
msgstr "Sa tutorial na ito, isinasaalang-alang natin ang trotterized na evolution ng transverse-field Ising model sa isang 1D chain na may nearest-neighbor na mga interaksyon:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"    H = \\sum_{\\langle i,j\\rangle}J_{ij}Z_iZ_j + \\sum_i h_i X_i\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"    H = \\sum_{\\langle i,j\\rangle}J_{ij}Z_iZ_j + \\sum_i h_i X_i\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To implement the time evolution $e^{-iH\\tau}$, we divide the time interval $\\tau$ into $r$ steps and define $\\Delta\\tau=\\tau/r$. The second-order Trotter-Suzuki decomposition gives the following:\n"
"$$\n"
"    e^{-iH\\Delta\\tau}\\approx \\prod_i e^{-ih_i X_i\\Delta\\tau/2 } \\prod_{\\langle i,j\\rangle} e^{-iJ_{ij}Z_iZ_j\\Delta\\tau} \\prod_i e^{-ih_iX_i\\Delta\\tau/2}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Para ipatupad ang time evolution na $e^{-iH\\tau}$, hinahati natin ang time interval na $\\tau$ sa $r$ na hakbang at dinedefine ang $\\Delta\\tau=\\tau/r$. Ang second-order na Trotter-Suzuki decomposition ay nagbibigay ng sumusunod:\n"
"$$\n"
"    e^{-iH\\Delta\\tau}\\approx \\prod_i e^{-ih_i X_i\\Delta\\tau/2 } \\prod_{\\langle i,j\\rangle} e^{-iJ_{ij}Z_iZ_j\\Delta\\tau} \\prod_i e^{-ih_iX_i\\Delta\\tau/2}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For circuit construction, each Trotter step is implemented as a sequence of single-qubit $R_x$ rotations and two-qubit $R_{ZZ}$ gates. The circuit begins by preparing the Néel state $|0101\\cdots\\rangle$ using X gates on alternating qubits. Each subsequent Trotter step applies: (1) $R_x(h_i\\Delta\\tau)$ on every qubit, (2) $R_{ZZ}(2J_{ij}\\Delta\\tau)$ on each neighboring pair along the chain, and (3) $R_x(h_i\\Delta\\tau)$ again on every qubit. The total circuit depth grows linearly with the number of Trotter steps $r$.\n"
msgstr "Para sa pagbuo ng circuit, ang bawat Trotter step ay ipinatutupad bilang sunod-sunod na single-qubit $R_x$ rotations at two-qubit $R_{ZZ}$ gates. Nagsisimula ang circuit sa paghahanda ng Néel state $|0101\\cdots\\rangle$ gamit ang X gates sa magkakahalinhinang qubit. Ang bawat sumusunod na Trotter step ay naglalapat ng: (1) $R_x(h_i\\Delta\\tau)$ sa bawat qubit, (2) $R_{ZZ}(2J_{ij}\\Delta\\tau)$ sa bawat magkatabing pares sa kahabaan ng chain, at (3) $R_x(h_i\\Delta\\tau)$ ulit sa bawat qubit. Ang kabuuang circuit depth ay lumalaki nang linear kasabay ng bilang ng mga Trotter step $r$.\n"

