"Nagtatakda rin tayo ng sumusunod na utility function, na nagbabalik ng halaga ng bit sa isang bitstring na `v` sa posisyong `i`. Halimbawa, kung `v = 6` (binary `110`),\n"
"- ang `bit_at(6, 1)` ay nagbabalik ng `0`,\n"
"- ang `bit_at(6, 2)` ay nagbabalik ng `1`,\n"
"- ang `bit_at(6, 3)` ay nagbabalik ng `1`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This follows the [little-endian convention](/guides/bit-ordering) used in Qiskit: the position `i` is indexed from the least-significant (the \"rightmost\") bit.\n"
msgstr "Sinusunod nito ang [little-endian convention](/guides/bit-ordering) na ginagamit sa Qiskit: ang posisyong `i` ay iniindex mula sa least-significant (ang \"pinakakanang\") bit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Small-scale simulator example {#small-scale-simulator-example}"
msgstr "Halimbawa ng maliit na simulator {#small-scale-simulator-example}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We consider a 1D chain of $N$ qubits, described by the transverse-field Ising model above. For the system of interest, we specify below the system size `N`, the Trotter step size `δt`, and the total number of Trotter steps `r_max`. The total evolution time is `δt * r_max`. Note that Julia supports Unicode identifiers such as `δt`; in the notebook or Julia REPL, type `\\delta` followed by Tab to enter `δ`. For a full reference, see the [Julia Unicode input documentation](https://docs.julialang.org/en/v1/manual/unicode-input/).\n"
msgstr "Isinasaalang-alang natin ang 1D chain ng $N$ qubit, na inilalarawan ng transverse-field Ising model sa itaas. Para sa sistemang pinag-aaralan, tinutukoy natin sa ibaba ang laki ng sistema na `N`, ang laki ng Trotter step na `δt`, at ang kabuuang bilang ng mga Trotter step na `r_max`. Ang kabuuang oras ng ebolusyon ay `δt * r_max`. Tandaan na sinusuportahan ng Julia ang mga Unicode identifier tulad ng `δt`; sa notebook o Julia REPL, i-type ang `\\delta` na sinusundan ng Tab para mailagay ang `δ`. Para sa buong sanggunian, tingnan ang [dokumentasyon ng Julia Unicode input](https://docs.julialang.org/en/v1/manual/unicode-input/).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Exact solution {#exact-solution}"
msgstr "Eksaktong solusyon {#exact-solution}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To establish a baseline for comparing results from the quantum hardware, we first demonstrate the classical simulation workflow for a small-scale problem. We build the Ising Hamiltonian as a sparse matrix, then obtain the exact time evolution by numerically integrating the Schrödinger equation using `ODEProblem` from `OrdinaryDiffEq.jl`. This approach scales exponentially in the number of qubits $N$. It requires storing the full $2^N$-dimensional state vector. For $N=20$ the Hilbert space already has over one million dimensions, making it impractical for larger systems.\n"
msgstr "Para makagawa ng baseline na maihahambing sa mga resulta mula sa quantum hardware, ipinapakita muna natin ang classical simulation workflow para sa maliit na problema. Binubuo natin ang Ising Hamiltonian bilang sparse matrix, pagkatapos ay kinukuha ang eksaktong time evolution sa pamamagitan ng numerical na pag-integrate ng Schrödinger equation gamit ang `ODEProblem` mula sa `OrdinaryDiffEq.jl`. Ang pamamaraang ito ay lumalaki nang exponential sa bilang ng mga qubit na $N$. Kailangan nitong itabi ang buong $2^N$-dimensional na state vector. Para sa $N=20$, mahigit isang milyon na ang dimensyon ng Hilbert space, kaya hindi ito praktikal para sa mas malalaking sistema.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We define the right-hand side of the Schrödinger equation in the in-place form `schrodinger!(dψ, ψ, H, t)`, which computes $d\\psi/dt = -iH\\psi$ using a sparse matrix-vector multiplication. We then set up an `ODEProblem` with the Néel state as the initial condition and solve it over the time span $[0, r \\cdot \\delta t]$, saving the state at each time step $\\delta t$. The solver used is `Tsit5()`, a standard explicit fourth/fifth-order Runge-Kutta method suitable for non-stiff problems.\n"
msgstr "Itinatakda natin ang kanang bahagi ng Schrödinger equation sa in-place na anyong `schrodinger!(dψ, ψ, H, t)`, na kumukwenta ng $d\\psi/dt = -iH\\psi$ gamit ang sparse matrix-vector multiplication. Pagkatapos ay nagse-set up tayo ng `ODEProblem` na may Néel state bilang paunang kondisyon at nilulutas ito sa saklaw ng oras na $[0, r \\cdot \\delta t]$, na sine-save ang state sa bawat time step na $\\delta t$. Ang ginamit na solver ay `Tsit5()`, isang karaniwang explicit na fourth/fifth-order Runge-Kutta method na angkop para sa mga non-stiff na problema.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "From the solution, which describes the state vector $\\psi(t)$, we can obtain the magnetization per site, expressed as the single-qubit $\\langle Z\\rangle$ expectation values as a function of time. We compare this with the results obtained from the Trotterized circuits.\n"
msgstr "Mula sa solusyon, na naglalarawan sa state vector na $\\psi(t)$, makukuha natin ang magnetization kada site, na ipinapahayag bilang mga single-qubit $\\langle Z\\rangle$ expectation value bilang function ng oras. Ihahambing natin ito sa mga resultang nakuha mula sa mga Trotterized circuit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Small-scale simulation of the Trotterized circuits {#small-scale-simulation-of-the-trotterized-circuits}"
msgstr "Maliit na simulation ng mga Trotterized circuit {#small-scale-simulation-of-the-trotterized-circuits}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In the following, we show the classical simulation of the noiseless circuits using tensor network methods supported by `TensorNetworkQuantumSimulator.jl`, so we can validate our circuit construction. These methods provide a baseline to compare with results from the quantum hardware.\n"
msgstr "Sa sumusunod, ipinapakita natin ang classical simulation ng mga noiseless circuit gamit ang mga tensor network method na sinusuportahan ng `TensorNetworkQuantumSimulator.jl`, para ma-validate natin ang pagbuo ng ating circuit. Nagbibigay ang mga method na ito ng baseline na maihahambing sa mga resulta mula sa quantum hardware.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We first define the lattice as a 1D chain graph using `named_grid((N,))`, where each vertex is a tuple `(i,)`. We then specify the circuit gates as a list of tuples `(gate_name, qubit_indices, gate_parameter)`, which serves as the input format for the tensor network simulator.\n"
msgstr "Una nating itinatakda ang lattice bilang 1D chain graph gamit ang `named_grid((N,))`, kung saan ang bawat vertex ay isang tuple na `(i,)`. Pagkatapos ay tinutukoy natin ang mga circuit gate bilang listahan ng mga tuple na `(gate_name, qubit_indices, gate_parameter)`, na nagsisilbing input format para sa tensor network simulator.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We use the belief propagation algorithm for tensor network contraction. This method is efficient for circuits with limited entanglement, but its accuracy degrades as entanglement grows with circuit depth. The `maxdim` and `cutoff` parameters control the trade-off between accuracy and computational cost. Similarly, we compute the magnetization at each site to compare later.\n"
msgstr "Ginagamit natin ang belief propagation algorithm para sa tensor network contraction. Episyente ang method na ito para sa mga circuit na may limitadong entanglement, ngunit bumababa ang katumpakan nito habang lumalaki ang entanglement kasabay ng circuit depth. Kinokontrol ng mga parameter na `maxdim` at `cutoff` ang trade-off sa pagitan ng katumpakan at gastos sa computation. Gayundin, kinukwenta natin ang magnetization sa bawat site para maihambing mamaya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1: Map classical inputs to a quantum problem {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"
msgstr "Hakbang 1: I-map ang mga classical input sa isang quantum na problema {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now we construct the Trotterized time-evolution circuit using `Qiskit.jl`. The circuit mirrors the tensor network version: it initializes the Néel state, applies $r$ Trotter steps of $R_x$ and $R_{ZZ}$ gates, and finally measures all qubits in the Z basis.\n"
msgstr "Ngayon, binubuo natin ang Trotterized time-evolution circuit gamit ang `Qiskit.jl`. Ginagaya ng circuit ang bersyon ng tensor network: ini-initialize nito ang Néel state, naglalapat ng $r$ Trotter step ng $R_x$ at $R_{ZZ}$ gates, at sa huli ay sinusukat ang lahat ng qubit sa Z basis.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We build a list of circuits for Trotter steps 0 through 10, corresponding to evolution times $\\tau = 0, \\delta t, 2\\delta t, \\ldots, 10\\delta t$.\n"
msgstr "Gumagawa tayo ng listahan ng mga circuit para sa mga Trotter step na 0 hanggang 10, na tumutugma sa mga oras ng ebolusyon na $\\tau = 0, \\delta t, 2\\delta t, \\ldots, 10\\delta t$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 2: Optimize problem for quantum hardware execution {#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"
msgstr "Hakbang 2: I-optimize ang problema para sa pagpapatakbo sa quantum hardware {#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To run on quantum hardware, the circuits must first be transpiled. This includes the following steps: select a set of physical qubits to map the circuit onto, recompile the gates into the native instruction set of the backend, and optimize the resulting circuit depth. We use `least_busy()` to automatically select the least-busy available backend, `target_from_backend()` to retrieve its native gate set and qubit connectivity, and `transpile()` to perform the compilation.\n"
msgstr "Para tumakbo sa quantum hardware, kailangan munang i-transpile ang mga circuit. Kasama rito ang mga sumusunod na hakbang: pumili ng set ng mga pisikal na qubit kung saan ima-map ang circuit, muling i-compile ang mga gate sa native instruction set ng backend, at i-optimize ang nagreresultang circuit depth. Ginagamit natin ang `least_busy()` para awtomatikong piliin ang pinakakaunting abalang available na backend, ang `target_from_backend()` para kunin ang native gate set at qubit connectivity nito, at ang `transpile()` para isagawa ang compilation.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "After transpilation, we inspect two properties of the compiled circuits. `get_circuit_layout()` returns the set of physical qubit indices selected for the circuit. `two_qubit_depth()` computes the two-qubit gate depth — the length of the longest chain of the two-qubit operations in the circuit — which is a useful indicator of noise accumulation on the hardware.\n"
msgstr "Pagkatapos ng transpilation, sinusuri natin ang dalawang katangian ng mga na-compile na circuit. Ibinabalik ng `get_circuit_layout()` ang set ng mga pisikal na qubit index na napili para sa circuit. Kinukwenta ng `two_qubit_depth()` ang two-qubit gate depth — ang haba ng pinakamahabang chain ng mga two-qubit operation sa circuit — na kapaki-pakinabang na indikasyon ng naiipong noise sa hardware.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Below we print the two-qubit gate count and circuit depth at each Trotter step; as expected, both grow linearly with the number of steps. Note that the fractional $R_\\mathrm{ZZ}$ gate is not yet available through the C API (see [qiskit-ibm-runtime-c#29](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit-ibm-runtime-c/issues/29)). As a result, each `RZZGate` is transpiled into two two-qubit gates instead of one, which inflates the two-qubit gate counts.\n"
msgstr "Sa ibaba, ipinapakita natin ang bilang ng two-qubit gate at ang circuit depth sa bawat Trotter step; gaya ng inaasahan, parehong lumalaki nang linear kasabay ng bilang ng mga step. Tandaan na ang fractional na $R_\\mathrm{ZZ}$ gate ay hindi pa available sa pamamagitan ng C API (tingnan ang [qiskit-ibm-runtime-c#29](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit-ibm-runtime-c/issues/29)). Dahil dito, ang bawat `RZZGate` ay itinatranspile sa dalawang two-qubit gate sa halip na isa, na nagpapalaki sa bilang ng two-qubit gate.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3: Execute using Qiskit primitives {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-primitives}"
msgstr "Hakbang 3: Patakbuhin gamit ang mga Qiskit primitive {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-primitives}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now we can submit the transpiled circuits to the backend as `Sampler` jobs with `shots` specified.\n"
msgstr "Ngayon, maaari na nating isumite ang mga na-transpile na circuit sa backend bilang mga `Sampler` job na may tinukoy na `shots`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As the jobs are completed, we can retrieve their results. Note that `get_sampler_job_results` function will block until the job is completed.\n"
msgstr "Habang natatapos ang mga job, makukuha natin ang kanilang mga resulta. Tandaan na hihintayin ng function na `get_sampler_job_results` hanggang matapos ang job.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 4: Post-process and return result in desired classical format {#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-format}"
msgstr "Hakbang 4: I-post-process at ibalik ang resulta sa nais na classical na format {#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-format}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "From the bitstring samples obtained from the quantum hardware, we compute the magnetization per site (the single-qubit $\\langle Z\\rangle$ expectation values) by averaging $(-1)^{b_i}$ over all shots, where $b_i$ is the measured bit for qubit $i$. We then plot the magnetization as a heatmap over qubits and Trotter steps, comparing the three methods side by side: exact classical simulation, noiseless tensor network simulation, and hardware execution.\n"
msgstr "Mula sa mga bitstring sample na nakuha sa quantum hardware, kinukwenta natin ang magnetization kada site (ang mga single-qubit $\\langle Z\\rangle$ expectation value) sa pamamagitan ng pag-average ng $(-1)^{b_i}$ sa lahat ng shot, kung saan ang $b_i$ ay ang nasukat na bit para sa qubit $i$. Pagkatapos ay ipinaplano natin ang magnetization bilang heatmap sa mga qubit at Trotter step, na pinaghahambing ang tatlong method nang magkakatabi: eksaktong classical simulation, noiseless tensor network simulation, at pagpapatakbo sa hardware.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The three panels below show the site magnetization $\\langle Z_i \\rangle$ as a function of qubit index (x-axis) and Trotter step (y-axis). At $\\delta t = 0.05$ with $r_{\\max} = 10$, the total evolution time is $\\tau = r_{\\max} \\cdot \\delta t = 0.5$, which is short enough that the initial antiferromagnetic pattern has not yet decayed — all three methods show a strongly alternating pattern. The classical and tensor network results are now in close agreement, confirming that Trotter error is small at this step size. The hardware results broadly track the other two, though some qubits deviate from the simulations more than others, reflecting variation in qubit quality across the backend. These deviations grow at later Trotter steps as the circuit depth increases.\n"
msgstr "Ipinapakita ng tatlong panel sa ibaba ang site magnetization na $\\langle Z_i \\rangle$ bilang function ng qubit index (x-axis) at Trotter step (y-axis). Sa $\\delta t = 0.05$ at $r_{\\max} = 10$, ang kabuuang oras ng ebolusyon ay $\\tau = r_{\\max} \\cdot \\delta t = 0.5$, na sapat na maikli kaya hindi pa nawawala ang paunang antiferromagnetic na pattern — lahat ng tatlong method ay nagpapakita ng malakas na magkakahalinhinang pattern. Malapit nang magkasundo ang mga resulta ng classical at tensor network, na nagpapatunay na maliit ang Trotter error sa laki ng step na ito. Sa pangkalahatan ay sinusundan ng mga resulta ng hardware ang dalawa pa, bagaman ang ilang qubit ay mas lumilihis sa mga simulation kaysa sa iba, na sumasalamin sa pagkakaiba-iba ng kalidad ng qubit sa buong backend. Lumalaki ang mga paglihis na ito sa mas huling Trotter step habang tumataas ang circuit depth.\n"

