# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Large-scale hardware example {#large-scale-hardware-example}"
msgstr "Halimbawa ng malaking hardware {#large-scale-hardware-example}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Steps 1–4 in a single workflow {#steps-14-in-a-single-workflow}"
msgstr "Mga Hakbang 1–4 sa iisang workflow {#steps-14-in-a-single-workflow}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We now combine all four steps above into a single workflow, at a scale beyond the reach of exact classical simulation. Instead of resolving the magnetization site by site, we track a single scalar measure of antiferromagnetic order, the staggered magnetization:\n"
"$$\n"
"    \\langle M_s \\rangle = \\frac{1}{N} \\sum_{i=1}^{N} (-1)^i \\langle Z_i \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Pinagsasama na natin ngayon ang lahat ng apat na hakbang sa itaas sa iisang workflow, sa laking hindi na maaabot ng eksaktong classical simulation. Sa halip na lutasin ang magnetization kada site, sinusubaybayan natin ang iisang scalar na sukat ng antiferromagnetic order, ang staggered magnetization:\n"
"$$\n"
"    \\langle M_s \\rangle = \\frac{1}{N} \\sum_{i=1}^{N} (-1)^i \\langle Z_i \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The alternating sign in the summation makes the signal visible. For the Néel initial state $|0101\\ldots01\\rangle$ every term contributes $+1$, so $\\langle M_s\\rangle = 1$, whereas the plain average $\\frac{1}{N}\\sum_i \\langle Z_i\\rangle$ vanishes identically for all $t$. As the transverse field scrambles the alternating pattern, $\\langle M_s\\rangle$ decays toward $0$, so the staggered magnetization tells us how much of the initial order survives during the time evolution.\n"
msgstr "Ang magkakahalinhinang sign sa summation ang nagpapakita ng signal. Para sa paunang Néel state na $|0101\\ldots01\\rangle$, bawat termino ay nag-aambag ng $+1$, kaya $\\langle M_s\\rangle = 1$, samantalang ang simpleng average na $\\frac{1}{N}\\sum_i \\langle Z_i\\rangle$ ay zero para sa lahat ng $t$. Habang ginugulo ng transverse field ang magkakahalinhinang pattern, bumababa ang $\\langle M_s\\rangle$ papunta sa $0$, kaya sinasabi sa atin ng staggered magnetization kung gaano karami sa paunang order ang nananatili habang nagaganap ang time evolution.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We also use this example to see how the Trotter step size affects accuracy. We fix the total evolution time $T = 1.5$ and vary the number of Trotter steps $r \\in \\{3, 6, 12\\}$, so that $\\delta t = T/r$. On hardware, two error sources compete: a smaller $\\delta t$ reduces Trotter error, but requires proportionally more two-qubit gates, which accumulate more hardware noise.\n"
msgstr "Ginagamit din natin ang halimbawang ito para makita kung paano nakakaapekto ang laki ng Trotter step sa katumpakan. Itinatakda natin ang kabuuang oras ng ebolusyon na $T = 1.5$ at binabago ang bilang ng mga Trotter step na $r \\in \\{3, 6, 12\\}$, kaya $\\delta t = T/r$. Sa hardware, dalawang pinagmumulan ng error ang nagtutunggali: ang mas maliit na $\\delta t$ ay nagpapababa ng Trotter error, ngunit nangangailangan ng proporsyonal na mas maraming two-qubit gate, na nag-iipon ng mas maraming noise ng hardware.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "At $N=100$ the exact solution from the ODE solver used above is out of reach, because the state vector alone would need $2^{100} \\approx 10^{30}$ amplitudes. Instead we use a noiseless tensor network simulation of the same 1D chain with a much finer Trotter step ($r = 96$, $\\delta t \\approx 0.016$) as the reference, where the Trotter error is negligible compared with any $\\delta t$ we run on hardware. This reference is itself approximate: its dominant error is now the bond-dimension truncation discussed above, reported as a truncation fidelity for each run.\n"
msgstr "Sa $N=100$, hindi maaabot ang eksaktong solusyon mula sa ODE solver na ginamit sa itaas, dahil ang state vector pa lang ay mangangailangan ng $2^{100} \\approx 10^{30}$ amplitude. Sa halip, gumagamit tayo ng noiseless tensor network simulation ng parehong 1D chain na may mas pinong Trotter step ($r = 96$, $\\delta t \\approx 0.016$) bilang reference, kung saan bale-wala ang Trotter error kumpara sa anumang $\\delta t$ na pinapatakbo natin sa hardware. Tinatayang halaga rin ang reference na ito: ang pangunahing error nito ngayon ay ang bond-dimension truncation na tinalakay sa itaas, na iniuulat bilang truncation fidelity para sa bawat run.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The plot below shows the staggered magnetization over time for the three Trotter step sizes, against the noiseless tensor network reference (dashed black).\n"
msgstr "Ipinapakita ng plot sa ibaba ang staggered magnetization sa paglipas ng oras para sa tatlong laki ng Trotter step, kumpara sa noiseless tensor network reference (putol-putol na itim).\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/time-evolution/extracted-outputs/94cd122e-0.svg)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/time-evolution/extracted-outputs/94cd122e-0.svg)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Overall, the coarsest Trotter step $\\delta t = 0.5$ (orange dots) shows the largest deviation from the tensor network reference, presumably with a large contribution from Trotter error. At the finer step $\\delta t = 0.25$ (green dots), the hardware results agree more closely with the reference. At the finest step $\\delta t = 0.125$ (purple dots), the Trotter error is smallest, yet the agreement is worse than at $\\delta t = 0.25$. With half the step size, each time point requires twice as many two-qubit gates, and the additional noise outweighs the reduction in Trotter error. Choosing $\\delta t$ for a Trotterized circuit on hardware is therefore a trade-off between Trotter error and the noise accumulated from additional gates.\n"
msgstr "Sa kabuuan, ang pinakamagaspang na Trotter step na $\\delta t = 0.5$ (orange na tuldok) ang may pinakamalaking paglihis mula sa tensor network reference, na marahil ay may malaking ambag mula sa Trotter error. Sa mas pinong step na $\\delta t = 0.25$ (berdeng tuldok), mas malapit na nagkakasundo ang mga resulta ng hardware sa reference. Sa pinakapinong step na $\\delta t = 0.125$ (lilang tuldok), pinakamaliit ang Trotter error, ngunit mas malala ang pagkakasundo kaysa sa $\\delta t = 0.25$. Kapag kalahati ang laki ng step, bawat time point ay nangangailangan ng dalawang beses na mas maraming two-qubit gate, at ang karagdagang noise ay lampas sa pagbaba ng Trotter error. Kaya ang pagpili ng $\\delta t$ para sa isang Trotterized circuit sa hardware ay isang trade-off sa pagitan ng Trotter error at ng noise na naiipon mula sa karagdagang mga gate.\n"

